# CI Pre-commit gate before commit / push

When changing files matching these globs (or when about to commit/push/PR any of them):

## Non-negotiable

Do **not** commit, push, or open/update a PR until:

```bash
pre-commit run --files <all-touched-paths>
```

passes locally. That is the same gate as CI’s **Pre-commit** job (ruff, ruff format, **mypy**, yaml hooks, etc.).

## Forbidden shortcut

- **Do not** treat `pytest` green alone as authorization to push.
- **Do not** skip mypy because “types look fine” or only unit tests were run.
- If pre-commit fails, fix and re-run; do not push a known red Pre-commit.

## Report before push

When offering commit/push/PR (or after the user asks to push), state that pre-commit passed on the touched files (or stop with the hook failure output).
